  Consequently there is no possible generalization of the construction of bad lines
and bad residual variables. We derive however from this result (Question and
Answer 1 above) some positive ones such as:
Theorem 2. Let R be a ring containing Q and m a positive integer. If f ∈
R[tm , tm+1 , · · · , t2m−1 ][x1 , · · · , xn ] is a variable of R[t][x1 , · · · , xn ] then it is a
variable of R[tm , tm+1 , · · · , t2m−1 ][x1 , · · · , xn ].

